  "step_3": "The decision reason requires focusing on the probability of the maximum possible outcome (2500 Euros) and preferring the option with the higher chance of that outcome (Lottery A, 33% vs. 0%). However, the individual does not mention the 2500 Euro outcome as a focal point or express any preference based on the likelihood of achieving the highest possible gain. Instead, they emphasize the downside risk (1% chance of 0) and the modest incremental gain. Their deliberation is loss-averse and certainty-seeking, not focused on maximizing the chance of the best possible outcome. There is no indication that they considered which lottery offers a better chance at the maximum outcome. Therefore, the reasoning process described does not align with the decision reason in focus.",
