  "step_3": "The decision reason evaluates which lottery has a higher probability of delivering its maximum outcome—here, A (34%) vs. B (33%)—and prefers A. The individual’s reasoning aligns with this in that they prefer Lottery A due to its higher chance (by 1%) of yielding a non-zero outcome, which is indeed its maximum outcome. Although the individual frames the justification in terms of avoiding zero rather than maximizing the chance of the best outcome, the underlying comparison involves the same probabilistic comparison of the maximum outcomes. The focus on the 1% increase in the chance to win 2400 Euros (the maximum of A) over 2500 Euros (the maximum of B) indicates that the individual is effectively attending to the probability of the maximum outcome per lottery. While the framing differs (risk avoidance vs. outcome maximization), the informational basis and the comparative logic match the decision reason. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used this reason, albeit with a different verbal framing.",
